    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"This publication includes maps and flightline databases of two detailed aerial gamma-ray surveys in the Albuquerque Basin, New Mexico.  These surveys were flown as part of a larger multi-disciplinary effort at the U. S. Geological Survey (USGS) to understand the hydrogeologic framework within the Middle Rio Grande Basin study area, comprised primarily of the Albuquerque Basin (Grauch and Millegan, 1998). The primary purpose of the surveys was to collect aeromagnetic data.  The aeromagnetic data were collected with the goal of mapping intra-basinal faults and intra-sedimentary lithologic variations that have bearing on ground-water resources.  The gamma-ray data were collected to test the usefulness of the data to aid geologic mapping.  In addition to maps of the gamma-ray data, this publication includes maps of aeromagnetic, topographic, and geologic data.  The purpose of this publication is to allow the user to interactively examine and compare the data in map and profile forms.  Refer to the introduction to the gamma-ray method for more information about the gamma-ray method.\r\n\r\nThe links on the bar above provide information regarding computer requirements, data installation, and a report based upon the report received from the contractor.  The links on the bar below provide information about this publication and the associated data.\r\n\r\nIn addition to the maps and descriptions of them, you can install a free viewer that provides interactive access to the maps and the flightline data.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
